{"sections":[{"chapter":"Colored Surface","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Color mode tokens control the colors used in colored surface components. In this chapter, we will override color mode tokens to customize the OUDSColoredSurface component."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"We will change the background color of the colored surface to match the Lime theme."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"title":"Colored Surface","projectFiles":"OUDS-Lime-Tutorial.zip","image":"ic_design_token_intro.png","xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.5","backgroundImage":"ic_design_token_intro.png","estimatedTimeInMinutes":10,"kind":"hero"},{"kind":"tasks","tasks":[{"anchor":"Overriding-color-mode-tokens","title":"Overriding color mode tokens","contentSection":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Color mode tokens are defined in "},{"code":"OrangeThemeColorModeSemanticTokensProvider","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". These tokens are special because they define high level rules of behaviors for colored surface like type of colors or monochrome mode."}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia","mediaPosition":"trailing"}],"stepsSection":[{"media":null,"caption":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The Lime theme uses a light green background for the colored surface. There is a semantic token of color which must be updated, and the provider of color modes tokens should refer to it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"code":"tutorial-lime-7.swift","type":"step","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Some token providers need references to others.","type":"text"}]}],"runtimePreview":"tutorial-lime-7.png"}]}]},{"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessments","assessments":[{"content":[],"type":"multiple-choice","title":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which component uses color mode tokens for its background color?"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"choices":[{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"para